# Vercel deployment ignore list.
#
# Vercel reads this file INSTEAD OF .gitignore when deciding which files reach a
# deployment. That distinction matters here: .gitignore excludes `dist/`, which
# is right for git (build output must not be committed) but was also excluding
# the compiled app from the serverless function bundle. tsc produced dist/ on
# the build machine and Vercel then dropped it, so at runtime the function
# failed with:
#
#   Cannot find module '/var/task/dist/src/app.js'
#
# dist is therefore deliberately absent from the exclusions below. Do not add it.
# The explicit re-include is belt and braces: if a Vercel version applied
# .gitignore *as well as* this file, the `dist/` rule in there would otherwise
# strip the compiled app again. Negation wins under git-style precedence, so
# dist ships either way.
!dist/**

# Reinstalled by npm ci; uploading it only slows the build.
node_modules
coverage

# Secrets. The deployment reads these from project environment variables.
.env
.env.*

# Android project: irrelevant to the web function, and large.
android

# Editor / OS noise and scratch output.
.git
.github
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
*.txt
.tmp-*

# Local preview artefacts.
admin-preview.log
do-prev.cmd
